# Fail-closed launcher only -- contains NO collector logic and is NOT a copy
# of dicks-lab-es-session.service. It does exactly one thing: if (and only
# if) dicks-lab-preflight-gate.service's marker exists, start the REAL,
# untouched, tracked production service via a plain `systemctl start`. If
# the marker is absent (preflight never ran, failed, or its marker could not
# be created), the Condition below fails, systemd marks this activation
# "skipped" (not failed), and the collector never launches -- fail-closed,
# no polling loop, no redesign of the collector. (0W-2 Attempt-5 design,
# unchanged in behavior by the 0W-2F marker-path correction.)
#
# 0W-4A: triggered by the recurring dicks-lab-launch-gate.timer
# (Sun,Mon,Tue,Wed,Thu 16:55 America/Chicago, immediately after the 16:42
# preflight). ExecCondition= (not ConditionPathExists=) so the check keeps
# the original fail-closed "skipped, not failed" semantics while actually
# validating the marker's payload equals *today's* America/Chicago date, via
# dicks_lab_gate_marker.sh check. A marker left over from an earlier trading
# date (or any date-content mismatch) fails the condition exactly like a
# missing marker -- no late catch-up launch, no stale cross-day
# authorization, regardless of how long dragon has been up.

[Unit]
Description=Dick's Laboratory — fail-closed launcher for dicks-lab-es-session.service
Documentation=file:/home/temckee8/Documents/REPOs/copper/docs/dicks_laboratory/FULL_SESSION_MULTIDAY_SOAK_REPORT.md

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecCondition=/home/temckee8/Documents/REPOs/copper/deploy/dicks_laboratory/scripts/dicks_lab_gate_marker.sh check /run/dicks-lab-launch-gate/preflight-ok
ExecStart=/usr/bin/systemctl start --no-block dicks-lab-es-session.service
